|
|  ● Verdict
|
|    The retry loop is correct, but the timeout is not applied to the retry itself.
|
|    ┌─────────┬────────┬─────────┐
|    │ attempt │ delay  │ outcome │
|    ├─────────┼────────┼─────────┤
|    │ 1       │ 250 ms │ retried │
|    ├─────────┼────────┼─────────┤
|    │ 2       │ 500 ms │ retried │
|    ├─────────┼────────┼─────────┤
|    │ 3       │ -      │ gave up │
|    └─────────┴────────┴─────────┘
|
|    • the delay doubles on each attempt
|    • the last error is kept as cause
|
|    ```ts
|      export async function withRetry<T>(run: () => Promise<T>, retries: number): Promise<T> {
|        // one call, then up to `retries` more
|        return run()
|      }
|    ```
